+
+## Current repair: constructive OR truth-table lessons
+
+- Version 1.1.2 sampled the two panels independently and only prevented a solid
+  union. It did not require left-only, right-only, and both-occupied aligned
+  cells, so plausible copy-left, copy-right, AND, or XOR rules could survive an
+  individual lesson. Controls were permissively coerced, `or_target` was not
+  exact over its declared domain, malformed ragged grids could crash
+  `self_check`, and there was no Python rule mirror or focused suite.
+- Version 2.0.0 replaces that sampler with a finite constructor. Every generated
+  example contains all four Boolean occupancy signatures, has an exact union
+  count, exposes four count profiles, supports exact 2–30 row controls, uses
+  strict nonzero distinct colors, and rejects unknown/ill-typed controls.
+  Difficulty now selects observable default height bands while explicit height
+  overrides retain the full declared range.
+- Added a strict `rule_mirror`, observable controls, canonical-pair parity tests,
+  boundary tests, finite-rival tests, and the reusable
+  `workspace/adversarial_review.py` protected-Racket audit.
+- Final focused suite: 78 passed. The audit checked 128 generated cases (127
+  unique inputs/outputs), four exact boundary cases, seven canonical pairs, six
+  executable rivals defeated on all 128 cases, and 27 protected-Racket labels.
+  This task remains catalog-unapproved and owner integration is pending.
